'' probe-ch14-scope-create.spin2  ->  isolate WHY ch14-scope-trace's SCOPE never opens
''
'' SYMPTOM (Stephen, 2026-07-26, PNut/Windows): running examples-library/ch14-scope-trace.spin2,
'' the TERM "Panel" window opens but NO SCOPE window appears. The TERM create is issued AFTER
'' the SCOPE create, so the program is running and the debug link is healthy -- only the SCOPE
'' create is being rejected.
''
'' COUNTER-EVIDENCE this probe has to explain: figure-generators/screenshots/
'' fig-14-scope-trace-scope_WDW.bmp (2026-07-11) shows a window titled "Trace - SCOPE" with
'' channel "Signal" rendered, produced by a BYTE-IDENTICAL create sequence. So either something
'' changed on the bench (PNut version, display scaling, window placement) or one token in that
'' create line is conditionally fatal.
''
'' METHOD -- five SCOPE creates that differ by exactly ONE thing each, all in one run, each fed
'' the same waveform, with a TERM narrating what was attempted. Windows are named A/B/C/D/Trace
'' (none is a debug keyword; the Jul-11 capture proves `Trace` is legal, this re-tests it anyway).
''
''   A      SIZE 400 220 only                    <- known-good shape; also clears SIZE height 220
''   B      SIZE + SAMPLES                       <- SAMPLES alone (ch07 proves this works)
''   C      POS 460 0 + SIZE + SAMPLES           <- POS+SAMPLES together, POS non-zero
''   D      POS 0 0 + SIZE + SAMPLES             <- POS+SAMPLES together, POS zero
''   E      SIZE + SAMPLES + POS (order swapped) <- is the parse ORDER-sensitive?
''   Trace  the EXACT failing line, byte-for-byte from ch14-scope-trace.spin2
''
'' DIFFERENTIAL FROM THE LIBRARY (2026-07-26): across all 34 examples, POS alone on a SCOPE
'' create works (ch14-multiwindow: POS 0 0 SIZE 400 200) and SAMPLES alone works (ch07 x3), but
'' POS *and* SAMPLES on the same SCOPE create line appears ONLY in ch14-scope-trace -- the one
'' that fails. C/D/E are the direct test of that conjunction; A/B are the controls.
''
'' The TERM window is created FIRST here (the example creates it last) so you have a running
'' narration even if every SCOPE fails.
''
'' WHAT TO REPORT BACK: which of the five SCOPE windows appeared. That single list isolates the
'' token. If ALL FIVE appear, our code is fine and the failure is environmental -- then re-run
'' figure-generators/fig-14-scope-trace.spin2 (known-good on 2026-07-11) to confirm.
'' Note: A and B are placed by PNut (no POS) and may land on top of each other -- drag them apart
'' before counting. D and Trace both sit at POS 0 0 and WILL overlap; drag the top one aside.

CON _clkfreq = 200_000_000

PUB main() | ang, signal, n
  debug(`TERM Log POS 460 260 SIZE 44 12 TITLE 'probe-ch14-scope-create')
  debug(`Log 0 'SCOPE create probe' 13 13)

  debug(`Log 'A: SIZE only' 13)
  debug(`SCOPE A SIZE 400 220)
  debug(`A 'Signal' -1000 1000)

  debug(`Log 'B: SIZE + SAMPLES' 13)
  debug(`SCOPE B SIZE 400 220 SAMPLES 256)
  debug(`B 'Signal' -1000 1000)

  debug(`Log 'C: POS 460 0 + SIZE + SAMPLES' 13)
  debug(`SCOPE C POS 460 0 SIZE 400 220 SAMPLES 256)
  debug(`C 'Signal' -1000 1000)

  debug(`Log 'D: POS 0 0 + SIZE + SAMPLES' 13)
  debug(`SCOPE D POS 0 0 SIZE 400 220 SAMPLES 256)
  debug(`D 'Signal' -1000 1000)

  debug(`Log 'E: SIZE + SAMPLES + POS (order swapped)' 13)
  debug(`SCOPE E SIZE 400 220 SAMPLES 256 POS 460 260)
  debug(`E 'Signal' -1000 1000)

  debug(`Log 'F: the exact ch14 line' 13 13)
  debug(`SCOPE Trace POS 0 0 SIZE 400 220 SAMPLES 256)   ' create with config only
  debug(`Trace 'Signal' -1000 1000)                       ' channel-def as a separate feed

  debug(`Log 'feeding all five...' 13)

  ang := 0
  repeat n from 1 to 300
    signal := qsin(1000, ang, 256)
    debug(`A `(signal))
    debug(`B `(signal))
    debug(`C `(signal))
    debug(`D `(signal))
    debug(`E `(signal))
    debug(`Trace `(signal))
    ang += 4
    waitms(10)

  debug(`Log 13 'DONE - count the SCOPE windows.' 13 'Expect 6: A B C D E Trace' 13)
  repeat                                   ' idle so the windows stay up
    waitms(1000)
